*  CN-15 / s170 -- THE s161 "LITERAL TWIN", RE-MEASURED AND RED.  FINDING-2026-08-19-s161 records
*  this shape as the exoneration of the final graph ("its literal twin (SPAN|SPAN) compiles and
*  passes m4").  At SCRIP f44be5f1 it CRASHES m4 (rc=139) on the default arm, for the same reason
*  cn_alt_leaf_flat_red does: the declaration statement's own ZLS slots push the match statement's
*  ALT-arm SPAN cells to +512/+528, past the live frame.  Nothing here is nested.
*  MEASURED s170: default arm m3 PASS / m4 rc=139.  SCRIP_SPAN_FRAME=1: PASS both media.
	&USER_DECLARED_CONSTANTS = 1
	&P = SPAN("ab") | SPAN("09")
	"ab" POS(0) *&P RPOS(0)	:S(Y)F(N)
Y	OUTPUT = "match"	:(END)
N	OUTPUT = "nomatch"
END
